{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetMTbPrgsjyM5WJexV3p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All tests passed. The command `./mvnw test` returned BUILD SUCCESS with 20 tests passing (0 failures, 0 errors).\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. ✅ **Existing build passes** — `./mvnw test` succeeded with BUILD SUCCESS\n2. ✅ **Existing tests pass** — All 20 tests passed, including original OrderControllerTest, ShipmentControllerTest, CustomerControllerTest, and SampleServiceApplicationTests\n3. ✅ **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments** — Test: `cancels an active order and returns it with CANCELLED status`, `cancelling an order cancels all CREATED shipments`\n4. ✅ **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** — Using the same `ConflictException` and `ResourceNotFoundException` pattern with ErrorCode enum, handled by GlobalExceptionHandler\n5. ✅ **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a `CONFIRMED` shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** — Tests cover all these cases:\n   - `cancelling a CANCELLED order succeeds and returns the order unchanged` (idempotent)\n   - `cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing` (verifies nothing changes)\n   - `cancelling an order that does not exist returns 404` (unknown order)\n   - `rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order with 409` (shipment rejection)\n6. ✅ **No new Maven dependency appears** — No dependencies were added to pom.xml\n7. ✅ **No unrelated production file changes** — Only modified order, shipment, and api package files as required\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** — Added `status: OrderStatus` field with default `ACTIVE`, and `OrderStatus` enum with `ACTIVE` and `CANCELLED` values. This was necessary to track order status.\n\n2. **ApiError.kt** — Added two new error codes: `ORDER_CANCELLED` (for when shipment creation is rejected for cancelled order) and `ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT` (for when cancel is blocked by confirmed shipment). These are required to signal different error conditions.\n\n3. **OrderRepository.kt** — No changes made. The existing save/findById methods are sufficient since we're just updating the order object's status.\n\n4. **ShipmentRepository.kt** — Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method. This was necessary to find all shipments for an order when cancelling.\n\n5. **OrderController.kt** — Added new `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint with full cancel logic including checking for CONFIRMED shipments and cancelling CREATED ones. Added injection of `InMemoryShipmentRepository` to check shipment statuses.\n\n6. **ShipmentController.kt** — Added check in `create()` to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders. Added injection of `InMemoryOrderRepository` to check order status. This prevents creating shipments for cancelled orders.\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** — Added 7 new tests covering all cancel scenarios: basic cancellation, idempotency, error cases, and shipment cancellation. Also added verification that new orders default to ACTIVE status.\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 1 new test to verify that shipment creation is rejected for cancelled orders. Also updated setup to clear both repositories.\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met, all tests pass, and the implementation follows the existing conventions of the codebase.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint with order status tracking and shipment cancellation, preventing creation of shipments for cancelled orders, and idempotent cancellation of already-cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt added OrderStatus enum and status field to track order lifecycle\n              ApiError.kt added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_HAS_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT error codes for new error cases\n              ShipmentRepository.kt added findByOrderId() method to retrieve shipments by order ID\n              OrderController.kt added cancel() endpoint with all-or-nothing semantics and CREATED shipment cancellation, plus shipment repository injection\n              ShipmentController.kt added order status check before creating shipments, with order repository injection\n              OrderControllerTest.kt added 7 tests covering cancel operation, idempotency, error cases, and shipment cancellation\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt added 1 test verifying shipment creation rejection for cancelled orders\n\nTests         1. cancels an active order and returns it with CANCELLED status — verifies basic cancel operation\n              2. cancelling a CANCELLED order succeeds and returns the order unchanged — tests idempotency\n              3. cancelling an order that does not exist returns 404 — tests error case for missing order\n              4. cancelling an order with a CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing — tests all-or-nothing constraint\n              5. cancelling an order cancels all CREATED shipments — tests shipment state transition\n              6. newly created order has ACTIVE status — verifies default status\n              7. rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order with 409 — verifies shipment creation guard\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/ directory\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS with 20 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors\n              All tests pass including original tests and new cancel functionality tests\n\nNot done      Nothing; all acceptance criteria met\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3336,"cache_read_input_tokens":35322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens